---
title: "Layout: tabsets and margin notes"
---

Taliesin renders tabbed panels and margin notes as web-native layout, and
cross-references resolve straight through them.

::: {.column-margin}
Margin notes float into the right margin on a wide screen and fall back to an inline
aside when there's no room. The same block works in posts, books, and sites.
:::

The same linear fit is shown three ways below: as Python, as R, and as a plot.

::: {.panel-tabset}

## Python

```python
import numpy as np

coef = np.polyfit(x, y, 1)
```

## R

```r
coef <- lm(y ~ x)$coefficients
```

## Result

![A linear fit through the sample points.](fit.png){#fig-fit}

:::

The fitted line is plotted in @fig-fit, defined inside the third tab above. The
reference still numbers and links even though its figure lives in a panel that is
hidden until you select that tab.
